.SH TARGETING A SPECIFIC INSTANCE
By default \fBamsg\fR prefers \fIASTEROIDZ_INSTANCE_SIGNATURE\fR when it names a
live socket, and otherwise falls back to the newest \fBasteroidz\-*.sock\fR in
\fIXDG_RUNTIME_DIR\fR. The fallback exists because the signature goes stale on
every compositor restart, so a tool that inherited an older environment would
otherwise fail silently against a dead socket.
.PP
That convenience is wrong for measurement. With several compositors alive \(em a
desktop session and a headless test instance, say \(em the fallback can answer
from one that is not under test, and a precondition asserted through it can
pass for the wrong reason. The following options make \fBamsg\fR refuse rather
than guess. Each has an environment equivalent so a harness can pin once and
have every later call inherit it.
.TP
\fB\-\-require\-pid=\fIN\fR (\fIAMSG_REQUIRE_PID\fR)
Fail unless the compositor that answers reports process id \fIN\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-require\-build=\fIHEX\fR (\fIAMSG_REQUIRE_BUILD\fR)
Fail unless its ELF build\-id matches.
.TP
\fB\-\-require\-session=\fINAME\fR (\fIAMSG_REQUIRE_SESSION\fR)
Fail unless its \fIDESKTOP_SESSION\fR matches.
.TP
\fB\-\-require\-validation\fR (\fIAMSG_REQUIRE_VALIDATION\fR)
Fail unless the Vulkan validation layer is loaded in it. Without this, a
\fBvalidation_errors: 0\fR reading is vacuous.
.TP
\fB\-\-instance\fR
Print the identity of the instance that would be used and exit.
.PP
When any \fB\-\-require\-*\fR option is given and \fIASTEROIDZ_INSTANCE_SIGNATURE\fR
is unset while more than one live socket exists, \fBamsg\fR reports an ambiguous
target and exits non\-zero. Picking the newest one is what produced a false pass;
under an explicit requirement, ambiguity is a failure.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fIASTEROIDZ_INSTANCE_SIGNATURE\fR
Path to the compositor's IPC socket. Set automatically by \fBasteroidz\fR(1).
If unset, \fBamsg\fR falls back as described above; if nothing is found it
prints an error and exits.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
\fB0\fR
Success (or help message printed).
.TP
\fBEXIT_FAILURE\fR
An error occurred (connection refused, send/receive error, etc.).
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBasteroidz\fR(1)
